Title:
Hades — Mythic C2 Chrome Extension Agent

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Hades is a post-exploitation agent for the Mythic C2 framework implemented as a Chrome (MV3) browser extension. It focuses on stealthy persistence and operating through browser/extension primitives rather than a traditional standalone implant. The agent communicates with Mythic over WebSockets and can optionally leverage a Python Native Messaging Host to reach OS-level capabilities. Core features include browser data collection (cookies/history/bookmarks/localStorage), SOCKS5 proxying through the victim’s Chrome context, filesystem operations, and arbitrary command execution via the native host. It also includes surveillance-style functions like screenshots, keylogging, clipboard access, and HTTP request/download monitoring. This is primarily useful for red teams and pentesters exploring browser-resident C2, proxying, and data access paths that blend into normal Chrome extension behavior.

Technical Focus:
- Chrome Extension Manifest V3 (MV3) agent design
- Chrome Native Messaging (Python host) for OS interaction
- WebSocket-based C2 communications with Mythic
- SOCKS5 proxying via browser/extension relay (socks_bridge)
- Browser artifact collection (cookies, localStorage, session export)
- Network/request monitoring and download interception via extension APIs

Use Cases:
- Establish persistence via a browser extension in environments where binaries are heavily monitored
- Pivot/proxy operator traffic through a victim’s browser using SOCKS5 (including leveraging victim cookies/session context)
- Collect browser-resident data (cookies, history, bookmarks, localStorage, sessions) for lateral movement and account takeover workflows
- Execute commands and perform file operations through a native messaging host on the endpoint
- Monitor HTTP activity and capture downloads for intelligence collection during post-exploitation

Keywords:
Mythic C2, Chrome extension, Manifest V3, WebSocket C2, Native Messaging, Python native host, SOCKS5 proxy, socks bridge, browser persistence, cookies, localStorage, session export, history, bookmarks, keylogger, screenshot, clipboard, HTTP request logging, download interception, post-exploitation agent